// cpp_alias_seed.ron — the curated `cpp` alias seed (REGISTRYLESS §3.2, §8, RL-6/RL-7).
//
// PROVENANCE — read this before trusting a row.
//
// C/C++ has no registry, so a build file never names a package: it names a
// *token* whose meaning is a convention of the build system that reads it.
// `find_package(ZLIB)`, `pkg_check_modules(zlib)`, a vcpkg port called `zlib`,
// and Debian's `zlib1g-dev` are four different spellings that all mean
// `github.com/madler/zlib`. This table is the hand-maintained mapping from those
// spellings to canonical stems. Every row is a *factual claim about upstream*
// and is independently checkable by opening the stem URL.
//
// These rows were authored by hand from knowledge of the upstream projects. They
// have NOT been bulk-imported from, or mechanically reconciled against, vcpkg's
// port index, Conan Center, Homebrew's formula API, or Repology — RL-7 forbids a
// bulk import, and no such reconcile has been run. Treat the table as a
// reviewed-by-one-author seed, not as an authoritative index.
//
// Known-fragile rows are the ones where upstream has *moved hosts* in recent
// years, because a stale stem is silently wrong rather than loudly broken:
//   - github.com/tukaani-project/xz      (was tukaani.org)
//   - github.com/pnggroup/libpng         (was glennrp/libpng)
//   - gitlab.com/bzip2/bzip2             (was sourceware.org)
//   - github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS    (was xianyi/OpenBLAS)
//   - github.com/uxlfoundation/oneTBB    (was oneapi-src/oneTBB)
// Re-verify these first when this seed is next reconciled.
//
// Deliberately omitted, because the token is genuinely ambiguous or upstream has
// no stable slug-shaped home, and a guess would be worse than an absence:
//   - `GSL`      — Microsoft's Guidelines Support Library vs. the GNU Scientific
//                  Library. Same token, two unrelated projects.
//   - `Curses`   — GNU ncurses' canonical home is a tarball site, not a repo.
//   - `Readline` — same.
//   - `GMP`      — same.
//   - Qt         — `find_package(Qt6)` fans out to dozens of per-module repos;
//                  one stem would misrepresent it.
//
// Invariants enforced by the tests in `ecosystem/cpp/alias.rs`:
//   - every entry is `curated` (feeds contribute `authoritative`, homepage
//     sniffing contributes `heuristic`; neither belongs in this file);
//   - every stem is either a `host.tld/owner/name` slug or `system/<name>`.
//
// `system/<name>` is for things that are not packages at all: they are provided
// by the toolchain or the platform, so there is no upstream repository to point
// at. Resolving `Threads` to a repository would be a category error.

[
    // ── CMake find_package tokens ───────────────────────────────────────────
